@p2050_split_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — The losing leadership wing, its named organisers and the exact departing caucus now appear as a political rupture; cabinet, opposition and caretaker positions are distinguished and every settlement has an authored result.
title: Poland 2050's parliamentary club fractures
subtitle: The defeated succession wing takes its mandates and leaves the new chair with the party name
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-new-deputies-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 34
order: 11
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 2 and third_way_split = 1 and p2050_formal_split_chain = 1 and p2050_joined_left = 0 and p2050_split = 0 and p2050_leader = "Katarzyna Pełczyńska-Nałęcz" and left_poll <= 12.5 and p2050_seats >= 3 and (p2050_coalition_dissent >= 24 or p2050_relation <= 35)
on-arrival: {!
Q.p2050_split = 1;
Q.p2050_split_occurred = 1;
const p2050SeatsBeforeSplit = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.round(Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0)
);
const splitShare = Math.min(
    0.60,
    0.24 +
        Math.max(0, (Number(Q.p2050_coalition_dissent) || 28) - 28) / 120 +
        Math.max(0, 30 - (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 30)) / 100 +
    Math.max(0, 12 - (Number(Q.left_poll) || 0)) / 80 +
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.party_system_left_pull) || 0) / 500
);
const centrumDefectors = Math.min(
    15,
    p2050SeatsBeforeSplit,
    Math.max(3, Math.round(p2050SeatsBeforeSplit * splitShare))
);
Q.p2050_split_defectors_2026 = centrumDefectors;
Q.p2050_seats = p2050SeatsBeforeSplit - centrumDefectors;
Q.centrum_seats =
    Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.centrum_seats) || 0)) +
    centrumDefectors;
Q.centrum_leader =
    Q.p2050_leader == "Katarzyna Pełczyńska-Nałęcz"
        ? "Paulina Hennig-Kloska"
        : "Katarzyna Pełczyńska-Nałęcz";
Q.centrum_defector_bloc =
    Q.centrum_leader +
    " leads the losing succession wing with Michał Kobosko and regional organisers";
Q.centrum_party_readiness = Math.min(
    7,
    3 + Math.round(centrumDefectors / 4)
);
Q.centrum_supports_government =
    Q.government_has_confidence && !Q.caretaker_government &&
    (
        Q.government_party == "p2050" ||
        Boolean(Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet)
    ) ? 1 : 0;
Q.news_headline = centrumDefectors +
    " Poland 2050 MPs follow " + Q.centrum_leader +
    " into a separate centrist caucus";
!}

= February 2026 — Arithmetic survives; trust does not

[? if centrum_leader = "Paulina Hennig-Kloska": <span class="party-p2050"><b>Paulina Hennig-Kloska</b></span>,
Poland 2050's green and cabinet-facing organiser, refuses the subordinate role
offered by the new chair.?][? if centrum_leader = "Katarzyna
Pełczyńska-Nałęcz": <span class="party-p2050"><b>Katarzyna Pełczyńska-Nałęcz</b></span>, the party's
state-capacity strategist, refuses to let the losing ballot erase her
organisation.?] <span class="party-p2050"><b>Michał Kobosko</b></span>, a former first vice-chair of Poland 2050,
brings European and regional contacts to the breakaway.

At the Sejm club meeting, **[+ p2050_split_defectors_2026 +] MPs** follow **[+
centrum_leader +]** out. They take their mandates, staff and committee votes;
they do not take the Poland 2050 name. The new caucus calls itself Centrum while
it decides whether it is a temporary shelter or the beginning of a party.

[? if centrum_supports_government: Both successor groups initially retain the
parent party's support for the cabinet. Every negotiation now has another
chair and another threshold calculation, but no new ministry appears.?]
[? if government_has_confidence and not centrum_supports_government: Both
successor groups remain outside the sitting cabinet; splitting an opposition
club does not manufacture government votes.?]
[? if not government_has_confidence: The split lands during a caretaker
period. Its two clubs are not fragments of a governing majority; they are
separate bidders in formation and election talks.?]

Lewica cannot appoint either centrist leadership or award Centrum a ministry
by recognition alone. It can accept the new parliamentary fact, spend political
capital on an orderly separation, or—if it shares government—turn the caucus
into an outside-support partner with no cabinet office.

- @center_split_accept
- @center_split_broker
- @center_split_ministries

@center_split_accept
title: Recognise two clubs and write separate parliamentary agreements
subtitle: Treat mandates as individual facts and make each caucus sign for its own votes.
on-arrival: {!
Q.p2050_coalition_dissent += 6;
Q.centrum_party_readiness += 2;
if (Q.centrum_supports_government) {
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 5;
    Q.coalition_status += " · two centrist caucuses";
}
Q.p2050_relation -= 2;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.centrum_supports_government
        ? "The cabinet now negotiates with two centrist caucuses"
        : "Lewica opens separate parliamentary talks with two centrist clubs";
!}

[? if centrum_supports_government: The cabinet receives two letters of support
where yesterday it had one. No minister changes party and no seat is counted
twice; every bill must now pass two centrist meetings. Poland 2050 resents
Lewica's speed in legitimising the caucus that wounded it.?][? if not
centrum_supports_government: Lewica opens separate talks with Poland 2050 and
Centrum without offering either a fictitious place in government. The split is
now legible in Parliament, and reconciliation becomes harder precisely because
both groups can function without it.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Recognise both clubs

@center_split_broker
title: Broker an orderly separation and a joint policy council
subtitle: Spend organisers on shared committee work and a truce over local structures, not a false reunion.
choose-if: resources >= 2 and p2050_relation >= 42
unavailable-subtitle: The factions no longer trust the Left as a neutral broker.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; p2050_coalition_dissent -= 8; government_coalition_dissent -= 4 if centrum_supports_government = 1; p2050_relation += 4; centrum_relation += 4; centrum_party_readiness -= 4; ko_relation -= 2; news_headline = "An orderly separation keeps both centrist clubs in a working accord"

**[+ p2050_leader +]** and **[+ centrum_leader +]** sign a separation protocol:
staff and local records are divided, joint bills receive a policy council, and
neither side may claim the other's MPs. Centrum remains a club, but the calm
settlement deprives it of the persecution story from which a new party might
have been built. KO again watches Lewica mediate the centre.

- @poland_event_queue: Sign the separation protocol

@center_split_ministries
title: Recognise Centrum as a separate outside-support caucus
subtitle: Add its votes to the support agreement without transferring a portfolio or pretending the split never happened.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
const centrumWasSupporting = Boolean(Q.centrum_supports_government);
Q.centrum_withdrew_support_2026 = centrumWasSupporting ? 1 : 0;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 3;
Q.p2050_relation -= 4;
Q.centrum_party_readiness += 3;
Q.barons_dissent -= 2;
Q.progressives_dissent += 2;
Q.public_trust -= 1;
Q.centrum_cabinet_status = "Separate confidence-and-supply caucus without ministries";
Q.centrum_supports_government = 1;
if (!centrumWasSupporting) {
    Q.government_support_seats = Math.min(
        Math.max(0, (Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460) -
            (Number(Q.left_seats) || 0)),
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) +
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.centrum_seats) || 0)
    );
}
Q.news_headline =
    "The cabinet records Centrum's outside support without inventing an office";
!}

Centrum signs a confidence-and-supply agreement in its own name. Only seats not
already recorded as supporting the cabinet enter the count, so the same MPs are
never manufactured twice. The caucus receives consultation, not ministries;
Poland 2050 now faces former colleagues bargaining from outside the cabinet.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the supply agreement
